## 20250424, 25

0.0.11: ~ GateIo::V4::Client#spot_orders: send only the arguments given, as strings; reset the timestamp after each request.

1. + lib/GateIo.rb: Hash#stringify_values
2. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#spot_orders: the arguments with nils dropped and every value a string.
3. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#do_request: @timestamp = nil after each request. The timestamp is memoised, so every later request through the same client was signed with the first one's.


## 20250207

0.0.10: /class GateIo/module GateIo/, + GateIo::Client, + GateIo::V4::Client#get, #post

1. ~ lib/GateIo.rb: /class GateIo/module GateIo/
2. + GateIo::Client, a subclass of GateIo::V4::Client.
3. + GateIo::V4::Client#get, #post: each a #do_request with its verb.
4. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#spot_currencies, #spot_currency_pairs, #spot_tickers, #spot_order_book, #spot_trades, #spot_candlesticks, #spot_my_trades, #spot_time: through #get.
5. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#spot_orders: through #post.
6. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#do_request: HTTP.send with the verb, in place of a case expression.


## 20250127, 0207

0.0.9: + GateIo::V4::Client#spot_orders

1. + GateIo::V4::Client#spot_orders: POST /spot/orders, taking currency_pair:, side: and amount:, and optionally text:, type:, account:, price:, time_in_force: and iceberg:.
2. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#do_request: a POST through HTTP.post where verb: is 'POST'.
3. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#message: + verb:; no query string for a POST, and any other verb raises.
4. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#encoded_payload: + args; the SHA-512 of the arguments as JSON, nils dropped, in place of that of an empty string.
5. ~ GateIo::V4::Client#headers: /Content-type/Content-Type/


